{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Re-review needed: the first review PASSED and signed at d74d53a5ffd, but one of its own findings was correct and should not have been dropped.\n\nThe G1G2 finding said the plan cites tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py, which does not exist. The gate vetoed it as cited-reference-inaccurate and dropped it. Verified independently: git grep -l init_ensures_seam returns nothing repo-wide, and ls tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py is No such file or directory. The file does not exist, so the veto was wrong and the finding stands.\n\nIt mattered in two places. The Context cited it as the pin for init._<name> reachability, and the Testing section listed it as a pytest target -- running that command verbatim would have errored on a nonexistent path, so the plan's own verification was a broken oracle.\n\nThe real pin is src/rebar/_store/ensures.py:93-100, which maps each unit name to init._<name>_unit (gc-config, merge-ours, gitattributes, gitignore, store-compat, untrack-runtime-markers), documented at that module's :14. The exercising test is tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py. Both citations now point there.\n\nThis edit invalidates the signature (plan_changed), so the plan goes back through review."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793474177296552001,"uuid":"5d8ad4d6-7e3b-4e5a-b5a6-4e6935e3a9ea"}